<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Chișinău</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Kishinev</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Chișinău, formerly Kishinev, is the capital and largest city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moldova">Moldova</a>. A small market town under the Principality of Moldavia, it became the administrative centre of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bessarabia">Bessarabia</a> after the Russian annexation of 1812 and grew rapidly in the 19th century; the pogrom of 1903 against its large Jewish community drew worldwide condemnation. In 1917 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sfatul-tarii">Sfatul Țării</a> met there and proclaimed the Moldavian Democratic Republic, and from 1991 it was the capital of independent Moldova.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/chisinau.jpg" alt="Chișinău" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Rodion Gavriloi · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Consiliul_Municipal_Chi%C8%99in%C4%83u_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
